{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791114591,"nonce":"qwjs7pjZICgqXUrvbKNIbXYId4I=","title":"Taffy 0.6: a non-shrinking flex item with a negative margin collapses its container's intrinsic width","message":"A row sized to its content (`flex-shrink: 0` on the row or not) comes out 0 wide when one of its items has `flex-shrink: 0` and a negative main-axis margin. Seen with the avatar group: three 40px avatars with `margin-left: -10px` on all but the first gave the group width 0 instead of 100, and the next sibling laid out on top of it.\n\nCause, taffy-0.6.3 `src/compute/flexbox.rs`, `determine_container_main_size`, max-content branch:\n\n- `content_contribution` includes the margin (40 - 10 = 30) and `flex_basis` does not (40), so `diff = -10`.\n- For `diff \u003c 0` the fraction is `diff / max(1, flex_shrink * inner_flex_basis)`. With `flex_shrink = 0` that is `-10 / 1 = -10`.\n- The contribution is then `max(1, flex_shrink) * inner_flex_basis * fraction = 1 * 40 * -10 = -400`, so the item counts as `40 - 400 = -360`.\n- The line sums negative and the container's main size clamps to 0.\n\nWith `flex_shrink = 1` the two factors agree (`-10 / 40`, then `40 * -0.25 = -10`), the item counts as 30 and the sum is right.\n\nWorked around in `components/css/components.css`: the group's avatars and its \"+N\" bubble are `flex-shrink: 1`. Nothing shrinks in practice, because the group is as wide as the overlapped sum.\n\nFix options: check whether a later Taffy release fixes the asymmetric scaling and upgrade; otherwise patch the scaling (use the same factor in both places), or report it upstream.","files":null}]}